      "description": "Watch Sunderland vs AZ highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 16, 2026. Sunderland and AZ faced off in a high-stakes UEFA Europa League clash on September 16, 2026, with both sides desperate to secure a vital victory under the lights. The match promised intensity and tactical discipline as the two European contenders met in a tightly contested affair. A Disciplined First Half Battle The game began with a high tempo, but it was characterized more by tactical fouls and defensive solidity than free-flowing attacking play. The referee was kept busy early on, issuing yellow cards to Sunderland 's Trai Hume in the 22nd minute and Omar Alderete in the 30th minute as the home side looked to assert their physical dominance. AZ were not without their own cautions, as Ayoub Oufkir was booked shortly before the break for a late challenge. Despite the territorial battle, clear-cut chances were at a premium during the first 45 minutes, leading to a goalless stalemate at the interval. The Decisive Moment from the Spot The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to break the deadlock. AZ introduced Weslley Pinto for Oufkir , but the substitute found himself in the book in the 65th minute after conceding a crucial penalty. This proved to be the turning point of the match. Enzo Le Fee stepped up to the spot in the 66th minute and showed nerves of steel, slotting the ball home to give Sunderland the lead. Immediately following the goal, the Black Cats made a triple substitution, bringing on Thomas Meunier , Brian Brobbey , and Nilson Angulo to provide fresh legs and defensive reinforcement. Late Pressure and Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, AZ pushed for an equalizer, introducing creative outlets like Calvin Stengs and Jizz Hornkamp . However, the Sunderland defense, bolstered by the earlier introduction of Daniel Ballard , remained resolute. Nordi Mukiele received a late yellow card for the visitors as frustrations grew. In the final minutes, Sunderland managed the game professionally, with Chris Rigg coming on to help see out the result. After four minutes of added time, the referee blew the final whistle, confirming a hard-fought victory for the hosts in front of a jubilant crowd."
